  "q0AnchorReason": "Experimental (proton) pin, the standing default. Q0 = Q_MP, imported transitively via hecke_channel_binding_probe, and Q_MP DOES track QOU_Q0_ANCHOR. CORRECTED 2026-08-26 (bean qou-1c4y). This previously declared `independent`, on the stated ground that running under QOU_Q0_ANCHOR=muon and =proton and diffing the witness showed \"the only non-ephemeral leaves that differ are q0Anchor and q0Value THEMSELVES -- every substantive field is byte-identical\". That experiment was re-run and REFUTES the claim: 43 non-ephemeral leaves differ, among them /E0_MeV and every entry of /channel_values_at_q0 for pp, nn and pn. Those are physics fields, not labels, so `independent` was false and the committed witness held the MUON value for q0. The CONCLUSION is unaffected: Pauli-complete is the best model under both anchors and the RMS values move by ~1e-8 relative, consistent with the 11.5 ppb muon-proton separation -- a correctness/hygiene re-pin, not a results-changing one, exactly as qou-1c4y predicts for this class. The earlier `muon` label was indeed a false claim; the fix is the honest pin, not a claim of independence."
